{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtREvwQFVTfF6vheSfQG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The direction was confounded, as I feared. The low-doubt class is dominated by math lines (36 of 131 are followed by \"$\", plus digits, \"No\", \"<think>\"), while the high-doubt class is prose bullet lines. A \"doubt direction\" from that contrast partly encodes \"prose line vs math line\", and ablating it could disrupt formatting. Also, the high-doubt points that do not continue with \"Wait\" continue with other doubt openers (\"Is\", \"Could\", \"What\"). So suppressing \"Wait\" alone (the n573 brake) would likely just change the opener.\n\nTo get a clean doubt contrast, I will restrict to prose line starts: positions where most of the predicted mass (>70%) is on alphabetic word openers. Among these, I compare lines where doubt words take most of the word mass with lines where commit/progress words dominate. If enough such positions exist, I will re-estimate the within-text direction there and check that it still separates held-out texts. If there are too few, I will need more teacher-forced prose junctions before any direction edit.\n\n```python\n# Cleaner contrast: prose-only line starts (word openers dominate); doubt share among word openers; counts and within-text direction quality.\ndef word_mass(t, b):\n    pw = pdub = 0.0\n    for j in range(20):\n        s_ = tok.decode([int(tki[t, b, j])]).strip(); p = float(np.exp(tkl[t, b, j]))\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"[A-Za-z][A-Za-z']*\", s_): pw += p; pdub += p * (int(tki[t, b, j]) in doubt_ids)\n    return pw, pdub\nwm = [word_mass(t, b) for t, b in zip(P_.t, P_.pos)]; P_['pw'] = [a for a, _ in wm]; P_['dshare'] = [d / max(a, 1e-9) for a, d in wm]\nprose = P_[P_.pw > 0.7]\nprint('prose points', len(prose), '| dshare quantiles', prose.dshare.quantile([.1, .25, .5, .75, .9]).round(2).tolist())\nprint('per text (n, hi>0.6, lo<0.2):', {t: (int((prose.t == t).sum()), int(((prose.t == t) & (prose.dshare > .6)).sum()), int(((prose.t == t) & (prose.dshare < .2)).sum())) for t in range(7)})\nprint('lo examples next words:', Counter(prose[prose.dshare < .2].word).most_common(10))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1311,"cache_read_input_tokens":162334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1311},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bffdcda1-9f39-489f-baee-e490968ea481","uuid":"8400917c-6d65-4af5-89d2-d86a0836e95b","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:58:27.958Z","request_id":"req_011CgtREupgSNdKpmcdntqDY"}
